[ledge] The two axial end faces of each centered 5 × 1 mm blade entry are the functional tool-access boundaries under the hooks. Tree(auto)/Default retains accessible supports at these small ceilings; post-processing uses a tiny flathead that fits inside the cavity. The slot does not cut the continuous spring wall.
alternatives: Filling the faces closes the blade entry. A ramped opening changes the flat screwdriver purchase and the remaining retaining bearing. Derek explicitly permits a tool and the extra edges for this release feature.
